 #'   b_shape))` hours. Worth fixing when the design cannot identify it, which
 #'   is the usual case with few observations per series; `mean_log_b_shape`
 #'   and `sd_log_b_shape` are then unused.
+#' @param start_dist Starting age distribution. `0` (the default) keeps the
+#'   wrapped symmetric Beta over the whole cycle, with one `b_shape` and
+#'   `b_offset` per `grp_init` group, exactly as before. `1` puts the
+#'   inoculum's ages at t = 0 on a Beta(`start_alpha`, `start_beta`) over
+#'   `[0, start_window]` hours since invasion, with no wrapping, and SHARES it
+#'   across every `grp_init` group, on the grounds that one inoculum was used
+#'   throughout; `b_shape` and `b_offset` are then absent from the model.
+#' @param start_window Width of that window in hours, required when
+#'   `start_dist = 1` and ignored otherwise. Must be below `min_cl`. For a
+#'   ring-only inoculum of 3D7, about 0.30-0.31 of the cycle.
+#' @param start_shape_cap Upper bound of the flat priors on `start_alpha` and
+#'   `start_beta`, whose lower bound is 1 (uniform over the window). A larger
+#'   cap pulls the prior toward narrower starts. Used only when
+#'   `start_dist = 1`.
 #' @param mean_log_b_shape,sd_log_b_shape,mean_log10_total0,sd_log10_total0
 #'   Per-`grp_init` priors, recycled to length `n_grp_init`. The
 #'   `log10_total0` pair is ignored when the inoculum anchor is in use.
@@ -125,6 +139,9 @@ archer_stan_data <- function(data,
                              mean_log_b_shape = 2,
                              sd_log_b_shape = 0.5,
                              b_shape = NULL,
+                             start_dist = 0L,
+                             start_window = NULL,
+                             start_shape_cap = 3,
                              mean_log10_total0 = 1,
                              sd_log10_total0 = 0.25,
